    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can ignore rotational symmetry with this question, since all circular permutations are rotational symmetric.  \n\nTo arrange 9 people in a linearly straight array, There are 9 possibilities for the first person. For each of these possibilities, there are 8 possibilities for the second person, 7 for the third, and so on. Thus the number of linear arrangements of 9 people is 9*8*7*6*5*4*3*2*1, or 362880.\n\nBut the circular arrangement can still be rotated, so we must divide by 9 to divide this number by 9 for each arrangement, and we must also take one configuration into account. The number of possible rotations of a given configuration is 9. \n\nThus the number of possible configurations is $362880/9/9,\\boxed{40320}$.",
